# A fold given its operator alone (card fold-bare-arguments, wiki/examples.md "folding")
'sum := fold +; sum [1 2 3]'	6
'product := fold *; product [2 3 4]'	24
'total := reduce +; total [4 5]'	9
'd := fold -; d [10 3 2]'	5
'fold [1 2 3] 0 +'	6
'fold [2 3 4] 1 *'	24
'reduce [1 2 3 4] +'	10
'xs=[5 6]; reduce xs *'	30
# an operator ending its line is the fold alone; the next line is the next statement (decision trailing-operator-indent)
'total := fold +\ntotal [1 2 3]'	6
'x = 1 +\n\t2\nx'	3
# a comparison alone as the order (card sorted-comparator-syntax)
'sorted([3, 1, 2], >)'	[3, 2, 1]
'sort([3, 1, 2], <)'	[1, 2, 3]
